<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jan Janszoon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1570–after 1641</span> · Also known as Murat Reis the Younger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jan Janszoon was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> privateer from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haarlem">Haarlem</a> who converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> after his capture by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> corsairs and became the corsair captain known as Murat Reis. Based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sale">Salé</a>, he served as a leading figure of the corsair Republic of Salé in the 1620s. His raids reached Iceland in 1627 and Baltimore in Ireland in 1631, carrying off captives for ransom or sale.</p></div>
